WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.134 --> 00:00:17.272
It was nearly summer and the weather was much warmer, but nobody at Patty's Place was smiling.

2
00:00:17.273 --> 00:00:24.027
It was exam time, and ahead were their final exams for the year and possibly their last exams ever!

3
00:00:24.028 --> 00:00:34.411
If they passed, Phil, Stella, Anne, and Priscilla would all be graduates of Redmond College and all holders of Bachelor of Arts degrees.

4
00:00:34.412 --> 00:00:39.396
"I wish I were dead, or that it was tomorrow night," groaned Phil.

5
00:00:39.397 --> 00:00:44.660
"If you live long enough, both wishes will come true," said Anne calmly.

6
00:00:44.661 --> 00:00:50.276
"It's easy for you to be calm," said Phil. "You can do philosophy.

7
00:00:50.277 --> 00:00:56.538
I can't! And when I think of that horrible exam tomorrow, I get so nervous."

8
00:00:56.539 --> 00:01:02.528
"You won't fail. How did you do in your Greek exam today?" Anne asked.

9
00:01:02.529 --> 00:01:08.305
"I have no idea! I've studied so much I can't think anymore!" said Phil.

10
00:01:08.306 --> 00:01:14.795
The busy days flew by, and when the examinations were over, Anne got first-class honors in English,

11
00:01:14.796 --> 00:01:20.882
Priscilla got honors in classics, and Phil got honors in math.

12
00:01:20.883 --> 00:01:26.702
On graduation day Marilla proudly attended the ceremony in Halifax.

13
00:01:26.703 --> 00:01:31.615
After Marilla left, Anne went home to Patty's Place to begin packing.

14
00:01:31.616 --> 00:01:36.136
"Just imagine, in one week, I'll be in Avonlea!

15
00:01:36.137 --> 00:01:42.679
How delightful!" thought Anne, bending over the box in which she was packing her clothes and belongings.

16
00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:51.523
"But imagine, in one week, I'll be gone forever from Patty's Place. How horrible!"

17
00:01:51.524 --> 00:01:55.473
Actually, Anne wasn't sure what the future held for her.

18
00:01:55.474 --> 00:02:01.037
If Roy proposed to her, everything would change, and he would definitely propose to her soon.

19
00:02:01.038 --> 00:02:04.375
Anne felt that she was truly in love with Roy.

20
00:02:04.376 --> 00:02:12.262
It was not exactly as she had imagined love to be, she admitted to herself, but Roy was a good man, and they would be happy together.

21
00:02:12.263 --> 00:02:17.906
"Is anything in life really the way you imagine it to be?" wondered Anne.

22
00:02:17.907 --> 00:02:25.312
That evening, when Roy came to Patty's Place and asked Anne to go for a walk in the park, everyone at Patty's Place knew why.

23
00:02:25.313 --> 00:02:31.635
And they thought they knew what Anne's answer would be. "Anne's a lucky girl," said Phil.

24
00:02:31.636 --> 00:02:35.905
"I suppose so," said Stella, shrugging her shoulders.

25
00:02:35.906 --> 00:02:40.744
"Roy is a nice fellow, but there doesn't seem to be too much in him."

26
00:02:40.745 --> 00:02:45.305
"Stella! Why do you say that?" demanded Phil.

27
00:02:45.306 --> 00:02:52.415
"I'm not being nasty; it's just that I worry Anne may end up unhappy," Stella explained.

28
00:02:52.416 --> 00:02:59.314
Under an old oak tree in the park—a very romantic spot—Roy asked Anne to marry him.

29
00:02:59.315 --> 00:03:05.968
His proposal was perfectly worded, as if he had copied it from a book, but it was also heartfelt and sincere.

30
00:03:05.969 --> 00:03:09.239
Anne felt that she ought to be thrilled from head to foot.

31
00:03:09.240 --> 00:03:13.434
But she wasn't; she just felt numb.

32
00:03:13.435 --> 00:03:18.903
Anne opened her mouth to say "yes," and then, suddenly, found herself trembling.

33
00:03:18.904 --> 00:03:24.076
She felt as if she were looking over a cliff, and then she had a moment of revelation.

34
00:03:24.077 --> 00:03:26.881
Quickly, she pulled her hand from Roy's.

35
00:03:26.882 --> 00:03:33.804
"Oh, Roy, I can't marry you . . . I can't . . . I can't," Anne cried.

36
00:03:33.805 --> 00:03:37.777
Roy turned pale. "What do you mean?"

37
00:03:37.778 --> 00:03:42.813
"I thought I could marry you, but I can't," said Anne desperately.

38
00:03:42.814 --> 00:03:47.160
"Why can't you?" Roy asked more calmly.

39
00:03:47.161 --> 00:03:51.609
"Because . . ." said Anne, "I don't care enough for you."

40
00:03:51.610 --> 00:03:59.861
Roy's face changed. "So you've just been amusing yourself with my affections this past year?" he asked slowly.

41
00:03:59.862 --> 00:04:08.052
"No, no, I haven't," gasped Anne. Oh, how could she explain? She couldn't explain.

42
00:04:08.053 --> 00:04:15.248
"Forgive me, Roy," Anne pleaded. "I did think I cared. Really, I did.

43
00:04:15.249 --> 00:04:20.392
But I know now that I don't." She looked at the ground.

44
00:04:20.393 --> 00:04:29.523
"You are not the woman I thought you were," said Roy angrily, and then with a bitter tone, "You are the only woman I can ever love.

45
00:04:29.524 --> 00:04:36.272
You've ruined my life. Good-bye, Anne." He stormed off.

46
00:04:36.273 --> 00:04:40.982
"Good . . . bye," Anne stammered too quietly for him to hear.

47
00:04:40.983 --> 00:04:45.927
She sat in the park, feeling drenched in shame and contempt.

48
00:04:45.928 --> 00:04:49.332
Anne slipped into Patty's Place and ran to her room.

49
00:04:49.333 --> 00:04:56.830
"I hope that no one will ever again ask me to get married as long as I live," she sobbed.

50
00:04:56.831 --> 00:05:01.686
Phil heard her crying and came in.

51
00:05:01.687 --> 00:05:07.835
"Phil," said Anne, "Roy asked me to marry him─and I refused."

52
00:05:07.836 --> 00:05:10.848
Her face was red with tears and shame.

53
00:05:10.849 --> 00:05:18.609
"You . . . you refused Roy?" said Phil blankly. "Are you crazy?"

54
00:05:18.610 --> 00:05:22.445
"Oh, Phil, don't scold me," Anne pleaded.

55
00:05:22.446 --> 00:05:28.785
"I honestly thought I cared, but at the last minute I realized I couldn't do it."

56
00:05:28.786 --> 00:05:32.264
"Well, Anne, I think you've treated Roy badly.

57
00:05:32.265 --> 00:05:36.925
You've been seeing him for a whole year!" said Phil in exasperation.

58
00:05:36.926 --> 00:05:40.325
Anne nodded, embarrassed, and started to cry again.

59
00:05:40.326 --> 00:05:44.514
The two stayed up talking until they both felt better.

60
00:05:44.515 --> 00:05:48.879
The next day all the friends at Patty's Place said tearful good-byes.

61
00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:56.294
Priscilla and Stella were glad that Anne had not accepted Roy's proposal and told her so. Anne felt slightly better.

62
00:05:56.295 --> 00:06:05.611
All the girls hugged each other, made promises to see each other again as soon as possible, and caught the train or ferry to their respective homes.

63
00:06:05.612 --> 00:06:10.914
When Anne returned to Green Gables the next day, everything was as it had always been.

64
00:06:10.915 --> 00:06:19.917
At dinner Marilla, Mrs. Lynde, Davy, and Dora caught up on all of Anne's life and filled Anne in on what had happened in Avonlea.

65
00:06:19.918 --> 00:06:26.902
They talked about who had gotten married, how the weather had been, and how the spring harvest had turned out.

66
00:06:26.903 --> 00:06:33.520
There was a short silence, and suddenly Davy remarked, "Hey, Anne, did you know Gilbert Blythe is dying?"

67
00:06:33.521 --> 00:06:37.758
"Davy, hold your tongue!" said Mrs. Lynde angrily.

68
00:06:37.759 --> 00:06:42.680
"Anne, don't look like that! We didn't mean to tell you so suddenly."

69
00:06:42.681 --> 00:06:48.093
"Is . . . it . . . true?" asked Anne in a voice that was not hers.

70
00:06:48.094 --> 00:06:52.452
Her face was so white that Marilla feared Anne was going to faint.

71
00:06:52.453 --> 00:06:57.151
"Gilbert is very ill," said Mrs. Lynde gravely.

72
00:06:57.152 --> 00:07:02.905
"He caught typhoid fever just after he arrived. It doesn't look good."

73
00:07:02.906 --> 00:07:08.966
Anne walked blindly across the kitchen, through the hall, and up the stairs to her old room.

74
00:07:08.967 --> 00:07:13.058
At its window she knelt down, staring ahead without seeing.

75
00:07:13.059 --> 00:07:26.160
The sky was very dark. Rain was beating down on the shivering fields. And Gilbert was dying . . .
